  "name": "FT4, TSH - ULTRASENSITIVE",
  "code": "FTSH",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"165\" data-end=\"491\">FT4 (Free Thyroxine) measures the biologically active fraction of thyroxine not bound to proteins. It reflects thyroid hormone status.<br data-start=\"321\" data-end=\"324\">TSH (Thyroid Stimulating Hormone, ultrasensitive) detects very low TSH levels and is highly reliable for diagnosing hyperthyroidism and monitoring thyroid disorders.</p>\n<p data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"522\"><strong data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"522\">Interpretation of results</strong></p>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_sk2ct_1\">\n<div class=\"_tableWrapper_sk2ct_13 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"1213\">\n<thead data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"580\">\n<tr data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"580\">\n<th data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"547\" data-col-size=\"sm\">TSH (Ultrasensitive)</th>\n<th data-start=\"547\" data-end=\"553\" data-col-size=\"sm\">FT4</th>\n<th data-start=\"553\" data-end=\"580\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Possible Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"639\" data-end=\"1213\">\n<tr data-start=\"639\" data-end=\"767\">\n<td data-start=\"639\" data-end=\"646\" data-col-size=\"sm\">High</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"646\" data-end=\"652\">Low</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"652\" data-end=\"767\">Primary Hypothyroidism (thyroid gland failure, e.g., Hashimoto&rsquo;s thyroiditis, post-surgery, iodine deficiency).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"867\">\n<td data-start=\"768\" data-end=\"774\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Low</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"774\" data-end=\"781\">High</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"781\" data-end=\"867\">Primary Hyperthyroidism (Graves&rsquo; disease, toxic multinodular goiter, thyroiditis).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"868\" data-end=\"947\">\n<td data-start=\"868\" data-end=\"874\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Low</td>\n<td data-start=\"874\" data-end=\"883\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Normal</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"883\" data-end=\"947\">Subclinical Hyperthyroidism (early or mild hyperthyroidism).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"948\" data-end=\"1026\">\n<td data-start=\"948\" data-end=\"955\" data-col-size=\"sm\">High</td>\n<td data-start=\"955\" data-end=\"964\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Normal</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"964\" data-end=\"1026\">Subclinical Hypothyroidism (early or mild hypothyroidism).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1154\">\n<td data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1049\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Low or Undetectable</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1049\" data-end=\"1055\">Low</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1154\">Central Hypothyroidism (pituitary or hypothalamic disorder causing inadequate TSH stimulation).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1213\">\n<td data-start=\"1155\" data-end=\"1164\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Normal</td>\n<td data-start=\"1164\" data-end=\"1173\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Normal</td>\n<td data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1213\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Euthyroid (normal thyroid function).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p data-start=\"1215\" data-end=\"1678\"><strong data-start=\"1215\" data-end=\"1237\">Key clinical notes</strong><br data-start=\"1237\" data-end=\"1240\">TSH is the most sensitive marker for thyroid dysfunction, especially in subclinical cases.<br data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1333\">FT4 is needed to determine severity and to differentiate subclinical versus overt disease.<br data-start=\"1423\" data-end=\"1426\">Interpretation should always consider clinical symptoms, medications (such as steroids, amiodarone, thyroxine therapy), pregnancy (trimester-specific reference ranges), and non-thyroidal illness (which can alter results without true thyroid disease).</p>",
